From 40b52d4b1dd503fc6fd9c61461d3f8c81ca38c4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vaibhaw1994kumar <vaibhaw01994@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:34:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Reserve worst-case legging exposure and bound residual in
 aggregate

- Package admission reserves the full leg quantity (not the flat net of a
  balanced package) against risk.max_legging_exposure_base, together with the
  residual carried from closed plans; new risk is refused while the carried
  residual is at max_residual_base.
- max_residual_base now bounds the total residual left open across plans: a
  plan that would push the total to the bound unwinds instead of closing with
  a naked leg. Offsetting residuals are accepted.
- Plan net_pnl marks the open residual at mid instead of booking the orphan
  leg's cash as PnL.
- OMS snapshot reports carried_residual_base and total_residual_base;
  monitoring alerts on the total and analyze-session warns on residual left
  at session end.

On recorded cycles 0006-0010 the replay now ends with <= 0.001 BTC residual
(was up to 0.007 vs a 0.002 bound) and net_pnl matches equity PnL within
0.2 USDT. 240 tests pass; run_all_local passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
